{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1260740-idigam-as-monster-factories","id":1260740,"title":"Idigam as monster factories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-15T13:25:03-07:00","id":1260740,"title":"Idigam as monster factories","content":"One of the primary abilities of all Idigam is the ability to create minions ( probably appropriate for werewolves who are designed to fight hordes) is there anything stopping them from just mass producing a supernatural army to march against the Uratha? Would it be appropriate to assume that they can create huge packs of their own to overwhelm whatever happens to bother them in a given area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T13:35:23-07:00","id":1260742,"title":"","content":"You mean asides from the time, energy, and resources needed to build, rein in, and direct such a horde?<br /> <br /> Not really. Other considerations might factor into it, such as a need to keep secrecy or such, but the big thing is the usual affairs of any horde building. They just have an easier time by skipping some of the time problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T13:39:11-07:00","id":1260743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1260740-idigam-as-monster-factories#post1260740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there anything stopping them from just mass producing a supernatural army to march against the Uratha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly their own wants. None of the idigam we've seen so far have been inspired by 'orderly werewolf genocide with masterminded tactics and strategy.' But there's also the fact that the Uratha aren't all located in one easily attacked location, like Prussia. And the more werewolves they gather the attention of the more likely the werewolves are to push back. Though if you're making an army you'll probably get more enemies than just the Uratha. Having spent the last few thousand years on the moon or hiding beneath the earth they are at the least entities that know some amount of fear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it be appropriate to assume that they can create huge packs of their own to overwhelm whatever happens to bother them in a given area? </div> </div> </div>They can change spirits around, claim people or werewolves with them. They can't make werewolves from nothing, they would have to get a pack and manage to 'Forge Empty Wolf' all of them but they could get the equivalent of a pack by doing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}